{
  "title": "Merits and Etiquettes of the Soil (Turbah) of Imam Husayn (a.s.)",
  "data": "Taking the Soil for Healing\nTake a piece of the soil no bigger than a chickpea with your fingertips, kiss it, pass it over your eyes and the rest of your body, and say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ بِحَقِّ هٰذِهِ التُّرْبَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA BIHAQQI HAADHIHIT TURBAH\nO Allah, by the right of this soil,\nوَبِحَقِّ مَنْ حَلَّ بِهَا وَثَوٰى فِيْهَا\nWA BIHAQQI MAN HALLA BIHAA WA THAWAA FEEHAA\nby the right of him who dwells in it and rests in it,\nوَبِحَقِّ جَدِّهٖ وَاَبِيْهِ وَاُمِّهٖ وَاَخِيْهِ وَالْاَئِمَّةِ مِنْ وُلْدِهٖ\nWA BIHAQQI JADDIHEE WA ABEEHI WA UMMIHEE WA AKHEEHI WAL A'IMMATI MIN WULDIH\nby the right of his grandfather, his father, his mother and his brother, and of the Imams from his descendants,\nوَبِحَقِّ الْمَلَاۤئِكَةِ الْحَاۤفِّيْنَ بِهٖ\nWA BIHAQQIL MALAA'IKATIL HAAFFEENA BIH\nand by the right of the angels who surround him:\nاِلَّا جَعَلْتَهَا شِفَاۤءً مِنْ كُلِّ دَاۤءٍ\nILLAA JA'ALTAHAA SHIFAA'AN MIN KULLI DAA'\nmake it a remedy for every malady,\nوَبُرْءًا مِنْ كُلِّ مَرَضٍ وَنَجَاةً مِنْ كُلِّ اٰفَةٍ\nWA BUR'AN MIN KULLI MARADIN WA NAJAATAN MIN KULLI AAFAH\na cure for every disease, an escape from every affliction\nوَحِرْزًا مِمَّاۤ اَخَافُ وَاَحْذَرُ\nWA HIRZAN MIMMAA AKHAAFU WA AHDHAR\nand a safeguard against whatever I fear and dread.\nThen use it.\nReciting [Surah Al-Qadr](A101) over the soil is its seal.",
  "tabs": [
    "Eating the Soil\nEat the soil only to seek healing, and no more than a chickpea; by precaution, no more than a lentil.\nWhen you eat it, or give it to someone to eat, say:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ وَبِاللّٰهِ\nBISMILLAAHI WA BILLAAH\nIn the Name of Allah (I begin) and in Allah (I trust).\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْهُ رِزْقًا وَاسِعًا\nALLAAHUMMAJ A'LHU RIZQAN WAASI'AA\nO Allah, make it ample sustenance,\nوَعِلْمًا نَافِعًا وَشِفَاۤءً مِنْ كُلِّ دَاۤءٍ\nWA I'LMAN NAAFI'AN WA SHIFAA'AN MIN KULLI DAA'\nbeneficial knowledge and a cure for every malady.\nاِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nINNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nVerily, You have power over all things.\nIt is better to put the soil in your mouth, drink a sip of water after it, and say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْهُ رِزْقًا وَاسِعًا وَعِلْمًا نَافِعًا\nALLAAHUMMAJ A'LHU RIZQAN WAASI'AN WA I'LMAN NAAFI'AA\nO Allah, make it ample sustenance and beneficial knowledge\nوَشِفَاۤءً مِنْ كُلِّ دَاۤءٍ وَسُقْمٍ\nWA SHIFAA'AN MIN KULLI DAA'IN WA SUQM\nand a cure for every malady and illness.",
    "Tasbih on a Turbah Rosary\nOn a rosary made of the soil, say with each bead:\nسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ وَلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَاللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ\nSUBHAANALLAAHI WAL HAMDU LILLAAHI WA LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WALLAAHU AKBAR\nGlory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Most Great.",
    "Dua al-I'tisam for Protection\nRecite it in the morning or the evening; in the evening, say \"Amsaytu\" (I have entered the evening) for \"Asbahtu\".\nHolding a rosary made of the soil, recite three times:\nاَصْبَحْتُ اَللّٰهُمَّ مُعْتَصِمًا بِذِمَامِكَ\nASBAHTU ALLAAHUMMA MU'TASIMAN BIDHIMAAMIK\nO Allah, I have entered the morning holding fast to Your protection\nوَجِوَارِكَ الْمَنِيْعِ الَّذِيْ لَا يُطَاوَلُ وَلَا يُحَاوَلُ\nWA JIWAARIKAL MANEE'IL LADHEE LAA YUTAAWALU WA LAA YUHAAWAL\nand to Your invulnerable shelter, which is neither overreached nor assailed,\nمِنْ شَرِّ كُلِّ غَاشِمٍ وَطَارِقٍ\nMIN SHARRI KULLI GHAASHIMIN WA TAARIQ\nagainst the evil of every oppressor and every night-comer\nمِنْ سَاۤئِرِ مَنْ خَلَقْتَ وَمَا خَلَقْتَ\nMIN SAA'IRI MAN KHALAQTA WA MAA KHALAQT\namong all whom You have created and all that You have created\nمِنْ خَلْقِكَ الصَّامِتِ وَالنَّاطِقِ\nMIN KHALQIKAS SAAMITI WAN NAATIQ\nof Your creatures, the silent and the speaking,\nفِيْ جُنَّةٍ مِنْ كُلِّ مَخُوْفٍ\nFEE JUNNATIN MIN KULLI MAKHOOF\nshielded against every terrifying thing\nبِلِبَاسٍ سَابِغَةٍ حَصِيْنَةٍ\nBILIBAASIN SAABIGHATIN HASEENAH\nby a full and impregnable garb,\nوَهِيَ وَلَاۤءُ اَهْلِ بَيْتِ نَبِيِّكَ مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ\nWA HIYA WALAA'U AHLI BAYTI NABIYYIKA MUHAMMADIN SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nwhich is my loyalty to the Household of Your Prophet Muhammad, Allah bless him and his Household;\nمُحْتَجِزًا مِنْ كُلِّ قَاصِدٍ لِيْۤ اِلٰۤى اَذِيَّةٍ\nMUHTAJIZAN MIN KULLI QAASIDIN LEE ILAA ADHIYYAH\nscreened from all who seek to harm me\nبِجِدَارٍ حَصِيْنٍ الْاِخْلَاصِ فِي الْاِعْتِرَافِ بِحَقِّهِمْ\nBIJIDAARIN HASEENINIL IKHLAASI FIL I'TIRAAFI BIHAQQIHIM\nby an impregnable wall, which is my sincerity in acknowledging their right\nوَالتَّمَسُّكِ بِحَبْلِهِمْ جَمِيْعًا\nWAT TAMASSUKI BIHABLIHIM JAMEE'AA\nand my holding fast to the rope of them all,\nمُوْقِنًا اَنَّ الْحَقَّ لَهُمْ وَمَعَهُمْ وَمِنْهُمْ وَفِيْهِمْ وَبِهِمْ\nMOOQINAN ANNAL HAQQA LAHUM WA MA'AHUM WA MINHUM WA FEEHIM WA BIHIM\ncertain that the truth is theirs, with them, from them, in them and through them.\nاُوَالِيْ مَنْ وَالَوْا وَاُعَادِيْ مَنْ عَادَوْا وَاُجَانِبُ مَنْ جَانَبُوْا\nUWAALEE MAN WAALAW WA U'AADEE MAN A'ADAW WA UJAANIBU MAN JAANABOO\nI befriend those whom they befriend, I am the enemy of those who are their enemies, and I shun those whom they shun.\nفَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهٖ\nFASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nSo bless Muhammad and his Household,\nوَاَعِذْنِيْ اَللّٰهُمَّ بِهِمْ مِنْ شَرِّ كُلِّ مَاۤ اَتَّقِيْهِ يَا عَظِيْمُ\nWA A'IDHNEE ALLAAHUMMA BIHIM MIN SHARRI KULLI MAA ATTAQEEHI YAA A'ZEEM\nand, O Allah, through them protect me from the evil of all that I fear, O All-great.\nحَجَزْتُ الْاَعَادِيَ عَنِّيْ بِبَدِيْعِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ\nHAJAZTUL A'AADIYA A'NNEE BIBADEE'IS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARD\nI have barred my enemies from me through the Originator of the heavens and the earth:\nاِنَّا جَعَلْنَا مِنْ بَيْنِ اَيْدِيْهِمْ سَدًّا وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ سَدًّا\nINNAA JA'ALNAA MIN BAYNI AYDEEHIM SADDAN WA MIN KHALFIHIM SADDAA\n\"We have set a barrier before them and a barrier behind them,\nفَاَغْشَيْنَاهُمْ فَهُمْ لَا يُبْصِرُوْنَ\nFA-AGHSHAYNAAHUM FAHUM LAA YUBSIROON\nand have covered them, so they do not see.\"\nThen kiss the rosary, pass it over your eyes, and say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْۤ اَسْاَلُكَ بِحَقِّ هٰذِهِ التُّرْبَةِ الْمُبَارَكَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA BIHAQQI HAADHIHIT TURBATIL MUBAARAKAH\nO Allah, I ask You by the right of this blessed soil,\nوَبِحَقِّ صَاحِبِهَا وَبِحَقِّ جَدِّهٖ وَبِحَقِّ اَبِيْهِ\nWA BIHAQQI SAAHIBIHAA WA BIHAQQI JADDIHEE WA BIHAQQI ABEEH\nby the right of the one buried in it, by the right of his grandfather, by the right of his father,\nوَبِحَقِّ اُمِّهٖ وَبِحَقِّ اَخِيْهِ وَبِحَقِّ وُلْدِهِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ\nWA BIHAQQI UMMIHEE WA BIHAQQI AKHEEHI WA BIHAQQI WULDIHIT TAAHIREEN\nby the right of his mother, by the right of his brother and by the right of his pure descendants:\nاجْعَلْهَا شِفَاۤءً مِنْ كُلِّ دَاۤءٍ وَاَمَانًا مِنْ كُلِّ خَوْفٍ\nIJA'LHAA SHIFAA'AN MIN KULLI DAA'IN WA AMAANAN MIN KULLI KHAWF\nmake it a remedy for every malady, a security against every fear\nوَحِفْظًا مِنْ كُلِّ سُوْۤءٍ\nWA HIFZAN MIN KULLI SOO'\nand a safeguard against every evil.\nThen place the rosary on your forehead.\nIf you fear a ruler or anyone else, do the same when you leave your home."
  ],
  "merits": "Many traditions, supporting one another, say that the soil (turbah) of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.), the earth of Karbala where he is buried, heals every disease and ailment except death, and gives security from every affliction and fear. The traditions on this are reported by so many that they cannot be doubted, and the wonders the soil has worked are too many to count.\n\nShaykh Abbas al-Qummi writes in his al-Fawa'id al-Radawiyyah, on the lives of the Shia scholars, that the great traditionist Sayyid Ni'matullah al-Jaza'iri endured much hardship in seeking knowledge. He was so poor that he studied by moonlight, until his eyesight grew weak. He then used the soil of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.)'s tomb, and of the tombs of the other Imams (a.s.) in Iraq, as an eye salve, and by its blessing his sight was restored.\n\nAl-Damiri reports in Hayat al-Hayawan, as al-Zamakhshari and others do, that when a serpent has lived a thousand years it goes blind, and Allah guides it to rub its eyes on fennel. However far it must travel from the desert to the gardens where fennel grows, it finds the plant, rubs its eyes on it and sees again. If Allah has put such healing in a plant, it is no wonder that He has put a cure for every illness, and other blessings, in the soil of His Prophet's grandson, who was martyred with his family, for the benefit of those who love him.\n\nSome of the traditions on the soil:\n\nThe women of Paradise (al-Hur al-'In), whenever they see an angel going down to the earth on some errand, ask him to bring them rosaries and prostration tablets made of the soil of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.)'s tomb.\n\nThrough a valid chain, a man said that Imam al-Reza (a.s.) sent him a bundle of clothes from Khurasan with some soil in it. He asked the messenger what it was, and he said: \"It is soil from the tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.). Whenever he sends clothes or anything else to anyone, he puts some of this soil with it, and he says: It is a security, by the permission of Allah.\"\n\nIbn Abi Ya'fur said to Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.), \"One man takes some of the soil of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.)'s tomb and it benefits him, while another takes it and it does not benefit him.\" The Imam (a.s.) said, \"No, by Allah: whoever takes it believing that Allah will benefit him by it, it will benefit him.\"\n\nAbu Hamzah al-Thumali asked Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) whether the soil that some of their companions took from Imam al-Husayn (a.s.)'s tomb to seek healing really heals. The Imam (a.s.) said: \"Healing is sought from the soil around his tomb up to four miles, and so it is with the soil of the tomb of my grandfather the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w.a.) and of the tombs of al-Hasan, Ali ibn al-Husayn and Muhammad ibn Ali (a.s.). So take of it, for it is a cure for every illness and a shield against whatever you fear, and nothing used for healing equals it except supplication. What spoils it is the vessels it is kept in and the little certainty of those treated with it; whoever is certain that it will heal him, it will heal him, by the permission of Allah, better than any other remedy. Devils and unbelieving jinn spoil it too, out of envy of the children of Adam. They cannot enter the Ha'ir, for the angels are there, so whenever soil is carried out of it, more of them than can be counted gather and rub themselves on it while it is still in its owner's hand, and its benefit is lost. Soil that escapes them heals whatever it is used for. So when you take it, keep it hidden and mention the name of Allah over it often. I have heard that some take it and think little of it, even putting it in the feed bags of camels, mules and donkeys, in vessels for food, for washing the hands after eating, or in saddlebags and sacks. How can someone who belittles it be healed by it? A heart without certainty spoils what it belittles of the very thing that is good for it.\"\n\nThe soil has other uses too. It is recommended to place some of it with the dead in the grave, to write with it on the shroud, and to prostrate on it. Prostration on it is reported to pierce the seven veils: the prayer is accepted and rises to the heavens. It is also recommended to make rosaries of it and use them for supplication and the remembrance of Allah, and merely holding one, without saying anything, brings a great reward (see [Rosary Made of the Turbah of Imam Husayn (a.s.)](I11)). Such a rosary glorifies Allah in its owner's hand, a glorification of its own, beyond the one Allah means when He says, \"There is not a thing but glorifies Him with His praise, but you do not understand their glorification\" ([Surah Al-Isra](A21), 17:44).\n\nImam al-Reza (a.s.) said that whoever says this tasbih with each bead of a rosary made of the soil, Allah records for him six thousand good deeds, erases six thousand of his sins, raises him six thousand ranks and records six thousand intercessions for him. Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that asking Allah's forgiveness once on such a rosary is counted as seventy times, and that whoever holds it in his hand without saying anything is counted as having glorified Allah seven times for each bead.\n\nDua al-I'tisam: in a valid tradition, when Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) came to Iraq, people asked him, \"We know that the soil of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.)'s tomb is a cure for every illness; is it also a security against every fear?\" He said that it is, and taught this dua with its rosary: whoever does it in the morning is in Allah's security until the evening, and whoever does it in the evening is in His security until the morning. Another tradition gives it as a protection for anyone who fears a ruler or anyone else, done when he leaves his house.\n\nThe scholars generally hold that eating earth or clay is forbidden, except the soil of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.)'s tomb eaten to seek healing, not for its taste, and no more than a chickpea, or by precaution no more than a lentil.\n\nAllamah al-Majlisi says that, by precaution, rosaries and prostration tablets made of the soil should not be sold but given as gifts, though there is no harm if both sides settle on an exchange without making it a condition in advance. Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) said, in a valid tradition, \"Whoever sells the soil of al-Husayn's tomb is as one who sells his flesh.\"\n\nMirza Husayn al-Nuri, Shaykh al-Qummi's teacher, tells this story in his Dar al-Salam. One of his brothers came to their mother, and she saw that he had put a prostration tablet of the soil in the side pocket of his robe. She scolded him for the disrespect, since it could end up under his thigh and break. He admitted that two had already broken that way, and promised not to do it again. Some days later their father, who knew nothing of this, dreamt that Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) came to him and sat in his study. The Imam (a.s.) was kind to him and asked him to call his sons, so that he might honour them. The five brothers came and stood before the Imam (a.s.), who had clothes and other things in his hand and called each of them in turn to give him a share. When that brother's turn came, the Imam (a.s.) looked at him with displeasure and said to their father, \"This son of yours has broken two prostration tablets of my soil under his thigh.\" Then he threw his share towards him instead of calling him up: as far as al-Nuri remembered, a comb used for weaving shawls (termeh). When their father woke, he told their mother the dream, she told him what had passed with her son, and he was amazed."
}
